WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.033 --> 00:00:01.568
Deadly fungal outbreak linked

00:00:01.568 --> 00:00:03.003
to a Michigan paper mill.

00:00:03.003 --> 00:00:05.205
Officials now say one person has died

00:00:05.205 --> 00:00:08.074
and there are 97 confirmed or probable

00:00:08.074 --> 00:00:09.709
cases of what is called

00:00:09.709 --> 00:00:11.411
blaster psychosis.

00:00:11.411 --> 00:00:12.245
All of the cases

00:00:12.245 --> 00:00:13.279
have been in Michigan's

00:00:13.279 --> 00:00:15.515
Delta and Menominee counties.

00:00:15.515 --> 00:00:16.883
The infection is caused

00:00:16.883 --> 00:00:19.252
by the fungus blast or misses

00:00:19.452 --> 00:00:22.188
It lives in mostly moist soil,

00:00:22.389 --> 00:00:24.391
soil and decomposing wood and leaves.

00:00:24.391 --> 00:00:25.291
And you can get it

00:00:25.291 --> 00:00:26.393
simply by breathing

00:00:26.393 --> 00:00:28.428
in the microscopic fungal spores.

00:00:28.461 --> 00:00:30.163
Joining us now is Brian Peterson.

00:00:30.163 --> 00:00:32.265
He's a vice president of operations

00:00:32.265 --> 00:00:34.434
at the paper mill there.

00:00:34.434 --> 00:00:36.436
I think that he is with us,

00:00:36.436 --> 00:00:37.670
although he may not be.

00:00:37.670 --> 00:00:39.406
Can you hear us

00:00:39.572 --> 00:00:40.974
You're there, okay?

00:00:40.974 --> 00:00:42.742
Yes, I can hear you just fine. Yes.

00:00:42.742 --> 00:00:44.110
Thank you so much for joining us.

00:00:44.110 --> 00:00:45.111
We really appreciate it.

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:46.913
Can you tell me we know that

00:00:46.913 --> 00:00:48.348
one person has died

00:00:48.348 --> 00:00:50.550
Have you been in contact at all with

00:00:50.550 --> 00:00:51.918
the contractors family?

00:00:54.754 --> 00:00:55.355
We have.

00:00:56.022 --> 00:00:57.457
I have not been in

00:00:57.490 --> 00:00:59.159
contact with the contractors family.

00:00:59.159 --> 00:01:00.527
We got news of that

00:01:00.527 --> 00:01:01.795
from the county last week.

00:01:01.795 --> 00:01:03.296
And we are just now getting involved

00:01:03.296 --> 00:01:05.031
in the investigation.

00:01:05.031 --> 00:01:07.767
When you worked in the mill in the last

00:01:08.101 --> 00:01:09.069
this year,

00:01:09.069 --> 00:01:10.036
what he was doing in the mill

00:01:10.036 --> 00:01:12.505
as far as work goes, that kind of stuff.

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:13.706
So we're cooperating

00:01:13.706 --> 00:01:16.342
with the investigation at this point.

00:01:16.709 --> 00:01:19.479
Do you know how people are getting sick?

00:01:19.712 --> 00:01:21.781
There are now some 100

00:01:22.082 --> 00:01:23.817
confirmed cases somewhere around

00:01:23.817 --> 00:01:25.485
97 to 100 confirmed cases.

00:01:25.485 --> 00:01:26.386
Do you know how they're

00:01:26.386 --> 00:01:27.821
they're getting it

00:01:29.989 --> 00:01:31.524
Unfortunately, we don't.

00:01:31.524 --> 00:01:33.693
Since we were first told of this

00:01:33.693 --> 00:01:35.695
from County Health in March 3rd,

00:01:35.695 --> 00:01:36.930
we've put a full court press

00:01:36.930 --> 00:01:38.131
on trying to understand it.

00:01:38.131 --> 00:01:38.731
And as you said,

00:01:38.731 --> 00:01:41.301
blessed with psychosis is in wet soil.

00:01:42.102 --> 00:01:42.869
It's our understanding

00:01:42.869 --> 00:01:43.837
from talking to CDC,

00:01:43.837 --> 00:01:45.572
there's no real other studies

00:01:45.572 --> 00:01:47.674
even close to this. And that's true.

00:01:47.674 --> 00:01:49.576
So we've invited a variety of experts.

00:01:49.576 --> 00:01:51.244
We're working towards the root cause.

00:01:51.244 --> 00:01:53.179
We invited niacin

00:01:53.179 --> 00:01:54.647
to do what's called a health

00:01:54.647 --> 00:01:56.049
hazard analysis,

00:01:56.049 --> 00:01:57.150
which they

00:01:57.150 --> 00:01:58.518
got the first phase of that done.

00:01:58.518 --> 00:01:59.252
And we're working through

00:01:59.252 --> 00:02:00.386
those recommendations.

00:02:01.387 --> 00:02:01.988
The next

00:02:01.988 --> 00:02:03.656
round of cleaning,

00:02:03.656 --> 00:02:05.325
we've decided to idle the metal to do.

00:02:05.325 --> 00:02:06.659
It's just too disruptive

00:02:06.659 --> 00:02:07.527
and there's too much risk

00:02:07.527 --> 00:02:08.461
to try to do the cleaning

00:02:08.461 --> 00:02:09.295
with people in the mail.

00:02:09.295 --> 00:02:11.164
So we are this morning

00:02:11.164 --> 00:02:12.632
or almost done in the mail

00:02:12.632 --> 00:02:14.767
and will commence with that cleaning.

00:02:14.767 --> 00:02:15.135
Okay.

00:02:15.135 --> 00:02:16.636
So you've idled the mill, you're

00:02:16.636 --> 00:02:17.070
clean, you're

00:02:17.070 --> 00:02:18.204
trying to clean

00:02:18.204 --> 00:02:18.705
to make sure

00:02:18.705 --> 00:02:19.606
the spores aren't

00:02:19.606 --> 00:02:21.174
in the air for people to get sick.

00:02:21.174 --> 00:02:22.175
Can you give me some sense

00:02:22.175 --> 00:02:22.509
of how

00:02:22.509 --> 00:02:25.011
the other 97 or so people are doing

00:02:25.512 --> 00:02:27.180
and what some of their symptoms might be

00:02:27.180 --> 00:02:28.414
Have you learned that

00:02:28.414 --> 00:02:30.216
in your investigation?

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:32.886
Well, I'm

00:02:32.886 --> 00:02:34.420
not an expert in blasting psychosis,

00:02:34.420 --> 00:02:36.289
although I'm getting there fairly quick.

00:02:36.289 --> 00:02:37.423
So I would encourage you

00:02:37.423 --> 00:02:38.324
to talk to the CDC

00:02:38.324 --> 00:02:39.292
about all the symptoms,

00:02:39.292 --> 00:02:40.293
because they can be

00:02:40.293 --> 00:02:41.327
quite broad but we've had

00:02:42.929 --> 00:02:44.430
people with very mild symptoms

00:02:44.430 --> 00:02:46.900
taking, taking medication and working

00:02:46.900 --> 00:02:48.101
just fine

00:02:48.334 --> 00:02:49.235
up until including you

00:02:49.235 --> 00:02:50.336
talked about the fatality.

00:02:50.336 --> 00:02:52.172
So it's a wide range.

00:02:52.172 --> 00:02:53.239
It has slowed down here

00:02:53.239 --> 00:02:54.040
in the last couple of weeks

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.575
as far as number of new cases go.

00:02:55.575 --> 00:02:57.043
But we are taking this

00:02:57.043 --> 00:03:00.446
with the utmost seriousness to go ahead

00:03:01.781 --> 00:03:02.882
and get

00:03:02.882 --> 00:03:04.617
get what we know out of these complex

00:03:04.617 --> 00:03:05.151
mostly around

00:03:05.151 --> 00:03:05.885
like ventilation

00:03:05.885 --> 00:03:06.886
systems, things like that,

00:03:06.886 --> 00:03:07.487
which are

00:03:07.554 --> 00:03:10.290
very hard to clean and bigger buildings

00:03:10.490 --> 00:03:12.392
in areas that were people were affected.

00:03:12.392 --> 00:03:12.992
I got to ask you,

00:03:12.992 --> 00:03:13.660
this is the first time

00:03:13.660 --> 00:03:14.727
I've heard about this

00:03:14.727 --> 00:03:17.130
and I know it exists in the world, but

00:03:17.664 --> 00:03:18.798
has this ever happened?

00:03:18.798 --> 00:03:20.366
Have you ever heard about this happening?

00:03:20.366 --> 00:03:22.168
At the plant, at the mill before

00:03:24.938 --> 00:03:25.672
No, I have

00:03:25.672 --> 00:03:28.875
never heard personally of any outbreak

00:03:28.875 --> 00:03:29.676
like this.

00:03:29.676 --> 00:03:30.243
You know, it is

00:03:30.243 --> 00:03:31.878
it is native to this part of the world.

00:03:31.878 --> 00:03:32.212
I can't say

00:03:32.212 --> 00:03:33.112
there's never been one,

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:33.913
but we're sure

00:03:33.913 --> 00:03:36.249
there's never been an outbreak like this

00:03:36.249 --> 00:03:38.284
in this mill or any mill that

00:03:38.284 --> 00:03:40.286
that we've been able to find.

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:41.754
And is there any sense

00:03:41.754 --> 00:03:43.056
that you believe that the spores were

00:03:43.056 --> 00:03:43.990
you know, in

00:03:43.990 --> 00:03:45.992
sort of wet paper or sort of

00:03:46.092 --> 00:03:46.593
some of the

00:03:46.593 --> 00:03:48.161
some of the items in the mill?

00:03:48.161 --> 00:03:50.230
Or is this coming from the outside in

00:03:54.767 --> 00:03:55.735
talking to the CDC?

00:03:55.735 --> 00:03:58.371
You know, because it's it's

00:03:58.371 --> 00:04:00.640
where it is originates from

00:04:00.807 --> 00:04:01.841
and it's airborne

00:04:01.841 --> 00:04:02.175
you know,

00:04:02.175 --> 00:04:03.409
we believe

00:04:03.409 --> 00:04:05.144
it had to come from outside somehow

00:04:05.144 --> 00:04:06.579
and then got into the air.

00:04:06.579 --> 00:04:06.813
I mean,

00:04:06.813 --> 00:04:08.481
if I look at all the affected cases

00:04:08.481 --> 00:04:10.350
or the affected people and employees,

00:04:10.350 --> 00:04:11.451
and then you start to map out

00:04:11.451 --> 00:04:12.518
where they work,

00:04:12.518 --> 00:04:13.386
you're really trying

00:04:13.386 --> 00:04:13.920
to understand

00:04:13.920 --> 00:04:14.320
where, where

00:04:14.320 --> 00:04:15.655
or what is in common

00:04:15.655 --> 00:04:17.257
with all of these employees

00:04:17.257 --> 00:04:18.524
or contractors.

00:04:18.524 --> 00:04:19.892
You know, where have they been in common?

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.961
So we can try to get the root cause.

00:04:22.028 --> 00:04:24.097
And that's really pushed us towards,

00:04:24.564 --> 00:04:24.764
you know,

00:04:24.764 --> 00:04:26.733
the areas that we're going to clean.

00:04:26.733 --> 00:04:27.867
This is people's work.

00:04:27.867 --> 00:04:29.902
This is how people make a living

00:04:29.902 --> 00:04:30.570
at the mill.

00:04:30.570 --> 00:04:31.371
Can you give us some sense

00:04:31.371 --> 00:04:33.039
of when the mill will be back

00:04:33.039 --> 00:04:34.407
fully functioning

00:04:34.407 --> 00:04:35.675
and safe enough for people to return

00:04:39.512 --> 00:04:39.912
You know,

00:04:39.912 --> 00:04:40.413
right now

00:04:40.413 --> 00:04:42.015
we're planning up to three weeks

00:04:42.015 --> 00:04:42.915
to get the cleaning done

00:04:42.915 --> 00:04:44.450
and we think we can get that done.

00:04:44.450 --> 00:04:45.451
It's a very dynamic

00:04:45.451 --> 00:04:47.220
and evolving situation, as you know,

00:04:47.220 --> 00:04:49.355
and so we have people

00:04:49.355 --> 00:04:50.857
as we're just getting the mill

00:04:50.857 --> 00:04:52.158
finished up idle this morning,

00:04:52.158 --> 00:04:54.627
we have experts that we worked with.

00:04:54.627 --> 00:04:56.329
They asked to get in the mill

00:04:56.329 --> 00:04:57.363
for the cleaning

00:04:57.363 --> 00:04:59.699
and we'll learn a lot as we go here

00:04:59.699 --> 00:05:02.068
in the next next few days.

00:05:02.869 --> 00:05:03.536
Brian Peterson,

00:05:03.536 --> 00:05:04.837
thank you so much for coming on

00:05:04.837 --> 00:05:05.672
explaining this.

00:05:05.672 --> 00:05:07.640
It is a really interesting

00:05:07.640 --> 00:05:10.043
and sad situation that's happened there

00:05:10.043 --> 00:05:11.144
at the mill with your employees.

00:05:11.144 --> 00:05:12.011
I appreciate your time.

